# You tell her something she did not know.
# {deed} the fact as she now knows it, {who} the girl it is about, {when}. {told} how it landed: good (she loves the
# news; your reputation goes up), neutral, bad (gossip about her friend or a mean secret; reputation and her trust drop).

@rule me.tell
on me.tell
- [Hey, did you hear?|Guess what I found out.|You won't believe this.|Okay, so, news.] [{Deed}.|{Deed}, {when}.]
- [Have you heard about {who}?|Don't tell anyone I said this, but...|So, about {who}...] [{Deed}.|Apparently {deed}.]
- [I heard something {when}.|Funny thing happened {when}.] [{Deed}.|Turns out {deed}.]
- [You know {who}, right?|Can I tell you something about {who}?] [{Deed}.|Well... {deed}.]
- [Promise you won't laugh.|Keep this between us.|Are you sitting down?] [{Deed}.|{Deed}, {when}.]
- [You're friends with {who}, so you should know.|I thought you'd want to know about {who}.] [{Deed}.|Apparently {deed}.]
- [I'm not one to gossip, but...|Nobody's talking about this yet, but...] [{Deed}.|Turns out {deed}.]
- [Word is going around about {who}.|People are saying things about {who}.] [{Deed}.|They say {deed}.]
- [I saw it myself {when}.|I only heard this {when}.] [{Deed}.|Well... {deed}.]

@rule tell.good
on tell
when told=good
feel surprised
hook f_tell_good
opens ask,laugh,agree
- [No way! Really?!|Seriously? {Who}?!|Wait, wait. {Who}?] [I had no idea!|I need to know everything.|You always know the good stuff.]
- [Oh my gosh.|Huh! Who would've thought.] [Thanks for telling me!|That's huge.|I'm so glad I heard it from you.]
- [Ooh, juicy!|Wow, okay!] [Tell me more later.|I won't say who told me.|You're my favorite source now.]
- [That's actually great news.|Ha! I knew it.] [Good for {who}.|I'll have to ask {who} about it.]
- [Hold on, say that again.|Are you sure about this?|Where did you hear that?] [This changes everything.|I've got so many questions.]
- [So that's what was going on.|That explains the look on {who}'s face.] [Thanks!|It all makes sense now.]
- [I can't believe I didn't hear this first.|How do you always hear these things first?] [I'm usually the first to know.|Teach me.]
- [I'm telling no one. Well, maybe one person.|My lips are sealed.] [Hehe.|Probably.]
- [You just made a boring day interesting.|Okay, this is the best thing I've heard all week.] [Got any more?|Thank you.]

@rule tell.good.couple
on tell
when told=good realverb=started_dating|crush|seen_together|kissed|dated|confessed
feel laugh
hook f_tell_good_couple
opens ask,tease,agree
- [Kyaa! {Who}?! Finally!|No way, {who} and...?!] [I knew something was going on!|They'd be so cute together!]
- [Oh, that's so sweet.|Ehh?! Since when?] [I'm a little jealous, honestly.|I have to see it with my own eyes.]
- [Stop, really?|Oh my gosh, {who}!] [I'm screaming inside.|That explains so much.]
- [Hehe, so that's why {who} was smiling.|Ha! I called it.] [Thanks for the scoop.|You're the best informant.]
- [Wait, {who} of all people?|I never would've guessed {who}.] [That's adorable.|Love is strange.]
- [Who made the first move?|Tell me it was {who} who asked.] [I need details.|I bet it was.]
- [Everyone's getting together except me.|Even {who}?] [So unfair.|I feel so left behind.]
- [I want to see the look on {who}'s face tomorrow.|I'm going to tease {who} so much.] [Hehe.|Don't stop me.]
- [No wonder {who} has been so distracted.|I noticed {who} checking their phone all day.] [That's why.|It all fits.]

@rule tell.neutral
on tell
when told=neutral
hook f_tell_neutral
opens ask,laugh,share
- [Huh. Okay.|Oh, really?|Interesting.] [I didn't know.|Good to know, I guess.]
- [Hm. Is that so.|Huh.] [Not my business, but okay.|I'll keep it in mind.]
- [Oh. Okay then.|Mm.] [People sure talk a lot.|Weird.]
- [I see.|Okay.] [Thanks, I guess.|Well, now I know.]
- [Everyone's talking about something.|There's always something.] [It'll blow over.|Not sure why it matters.]
- [I guess that happens.|Sounds like {who}.] [Okay.|Nothing new.]
- [Did you hear that from someone reliable?|Are you sure?] [I'll wait and see.|Hm.]
- [Should I be surprised?|Is that supposed to be big news?] [Sorry.|I'm not really shocked.]
- [That's nice for {who}, I guess.|Well, good luck to {who}.] [Moving on.|Anyway.]

@rule tell.neutral.cool
on tell
when told=neutral voice=cool|serious|proper
hook f_tell_neutral_cool
opens ask,share
- [I see.|Hm.] [I don't usually follow gossip.|That's their business.]
- [Is that so.|Noted.] [I'll not repeat it.|Why tell me, though?]
- [Hm. Interesting.|Huh.] [People's lives are complicated.|I suppose it was bound to happen.]
- [That's... a lot of detail.|You hear everything, huh.] [I'll pretend I didn't.|Okay.]
- [I had already guessed.|That isn't surprising.] [The signs were there.|People are predictable.]
- [What {who} does is no concern of mine.|I don't see how that involves me.] [Is there anything else?|Hm.]
- [You seem to enjoy this.|You collect these stories, don't you?] [Curious hobby.|Hm.]
- [Your source may be unreliable.|That sounds exaggerated.] [I'll reserve judgment.|We'll see.]
- [Thank you for the information. I think.|Very well. Now I'm informed.] [Hm.|Good.]

@rule tell.bad
on tell
when told=bad
feel pout
hook f_tell_bad
opens hush,defend,laugh
- [Why are you telling me this?|That's not something you spread around.|That's mean, you know.] [{Who} wouldn't want people knowing.|I didn't need to hear that.]
- [Wow. Talking behind {who}'s back?|Is that how you talk about people?] [What do you say about me, then?|I don't like this.]
- [{Who}'s my friend.|Hey, careful.] [I'm not passing that on.|Don't tell anyone else.]
- [That's gossip. Mean gossip.|Ugh.] [I thought better of you.|Let's not.]
- [Would you say that to {who}'s face?|Does {who} know you go around saying that?] [Didn't think so.|Think about it.]
- [That could really hurt {who}.|Rumors like that follow people around.] [Think before you talk.|Stop it.]
- [I don't want to be part of this.|Leave me out of it.] [Seriously.|Find someone else to tell.]
- [What's your problem with {who}?|What did {who} ever do to you?] [Honestly.|Well?]
- [And if it's not even true?|You don't know the whole story.] [Then what?|Neither do I.]

@rule tell.bad.friend
on tell
when told=bad whobond>=40
feel sad
hook f_tell_bad_friend
opens hush,defend
- [{Who}...? Oh no.|Poor {who}.] [I should go check on her.|Why didn't she tell me?]
- [You're telling me this about {who}? My friend?|That's my friend you're talking about.] [Not cool.|I'll hear it from her, thanks.]
- [I don't believe it.|That can't be right.] [{Who} would never.|You'd better not spread that.]
- [That's awful.|Ugh, I hate this.] [Please don't tell anyone else.|Let me talk to {who} first.]
- [{Who} trusted people here.|{Who} doesn't deserve this.] [I can't believe it.|This isn't fair.]
- [If this gets back to {who}, I'll know it was you.|I'm going to tell {who} what you said.] [Remember that.|Don't look at me like that.]
- [Did someone put you up to this?|Who else have you told about {who}?] [Tell me the truth.|Tell me.]
- [I've known {who} for a long time.|I know {who} better than you do.] [It's not like that.|So stop.]
- [I need to go find {who}.|Sorry, I can't talk about {who} like this.] [Excuse me.|Not with you.]
